'''''Scilla monophyllos''''', the '''single-leaved squill''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Asparagaceae]].<ref name="RHS_16854" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/16854/scilla-monophyllos/details |title=''Scilla monophyllos'' single-leaved squill |author=<!--Not stated-->|date=2025 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=7 March 2025 |quote=1 suppliers }}</ref> It is native to Morocco, Portugal, and western Spain.<ref name="POWO_540925-1" >{{cite POWO |id=540925-1 |title=''Scilla monophyllos'' Link |access-date=7 March 2025 }}</ref> As its scientific and common names suggest, it typically has only one leaf.<ref name="RHS_16854" />
